<title>USA: Hosposable Products Q4 net loss widens.</title>
<headline>Hosposable Products Q4 net loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>SOMERVILLE, N.J. 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>THREE MONTHS ENDED DECEMBER 31</p>
<p>						    1996		1995</p>
<p> Net sales				$10,422,096     $10,415,588</p>
<p> Net loss				   (642,002)	 (508,293)</p>
<p> Net loss per share			   (.38)	     (.30)</p>
<p> Weighted average shares		1,692,476	 1,692,476</p>
<p>						  YEAR ENDED DECEMBER 31</p>
<p>						     1996	     1995</p>
<p> Net sales				$42,293,633     $40,480,738</p>
<p> Net loss				 (1,055,190)	 (209,206)</p>
<p> Net loss per share			   (.62)	     (.12)</p>
<p> Weighted average shares		1,692,476	 1,692,476</p>
<p>NOTE:  Hosposable Products Inc said its net loss for 1996 includes a pre-tax charge of $549,805 ($350,000 or $.21 per share after-tax) for professional services in connection with the acquisition of the Canadian operations of G. H. Wood + Wyant Inc.</p>
<p>The 1995 net loss includes a pre-tax charge of $550,000 ($340,000 or $.20 per share after-tax) for the writedown of machinery and equipment, leasehold improvements and leased space not being utilized for operations.</p>
</text>
